These are all OSF/1 MIPS based (and it's OSF/1 from OSF using the
OSF/rose object format, rather than OSF/1 from DEC using the ECOFF
object format).  The gcc is certainly obsolete (all of the changes are
folded into the standard 2.3.3 release).  The assembler and linker are
only of interest if you have OSF/rose (and soon will be obsolete
also).
