I've built it, I haven't got all the bugs out yet, but it works okish.

Unfortunately I don't have diffs, so what follows is a description of
what you need to do...

1) find the calls to sysv_getc (there's only a couple) and change the
   #ifdefs wrapped round them to enable them on the alpha

2) make sure that there are function protoypes for all functions
   returning pointers available to all the files that use them...
   (this is ongoing for me, I have undoubtedly missed some but haven't
   the time to do the job properly at present). In particular, you
   need to make sure that the parser includes command.h and that this
   has declarations for all the make_xxx_command routines. You can use
   the -proto option on the C compiler as a cheap'n'easy way to
   generate function prototypes from the C files - unfortunately
   theres no one to one correspondance between the C files and the
   header files to make it easy to decide where the declarations
   should go :-(.


If you sort things out more formally and carefully than I've managed,
or need further help, there should be an address to send email to in
the README or INSTALL files in your distribution.

Good luck...


 


