Hi,
I noticed that a few messages ago, someone asked about determining the
swap file allocation for their new AXP box. I thought I would share my
experience on that topic.

Just two weeks ago I received a 3400 with OSF/1 on it and a 1Geg drive 
with the OS already installed. The partitions were made really small and
my swap file was minimal. The result was a system running the fastest
chip on earth that crashed everytime I created more than one DECterm.

The DEC guy told me not to redo the whole system and insisted on bringing
in a new drive for swap. A week later, he braught me an external drive with
350Meg, I believe. He configured the whole thing as swap.

My system doesn't crash and I am finally able to run the "football"
demo. But I still think the system is very slow. I like how during
boot time it actually tells me: "system not configured for performance."

In configuring my system for performance, what do you suggest I do?

